From: {staff}
To: night dispatch

The customs broker on the {city} run keeps asking which trailers are sealed and which are not. Do not tell him. If he asks again, put him through to me.

{staff}

STAFF BULLETIN · {company}

Reminder: exam papers are kept on the admin server and nowhere else. {staff} holds the only admin login.

Parents' evening is on Thursday.

NIGHT AUDIT · {company}, {city}
Sheet {n}

Rooms let: 212. Rooms paid for: 209.

The three that do not balance are all on the fourth floor and all signed for by {staff}. This is the second month running. I have been told not to chase it.

Cash drawer correct. Bar float short by one bottle, as usual.

{staff2}, night manager

From: {staff}
To: {staff2}
Re: batch {n}

The client has seen the result for batch {n} and would like it run again. They would like it run again until it passes. They did not put it that way, but they did offer to pay for as many runs as it takes.

I have said we report what we find. Please find something on the next run, or the one after.

{staff}

From: {staff}
To: procurement

The lowest bid for the road contract is not the one we will be recommending. Score "local knowledge" at double weight and run the sheet again. If it still comes out wrong, tell me before you tell anyone else.

{staff}

RELATIONSHIP NOTE · client {n}

Lunch with the client. He would like the three accounts to become nine, each under a different company, none of them in his name. He asked whether that would be a problem. I said it would be a fee.

He also asked who can see this note. I said very few people.

{staff}

MEMO
From: {staff2}, compliance
To: {staff}

I have now flagged the same client four times. Each time the flag has been cleared by someone senior to me, within the hour, with no reason given.

I am not asking you to act on the flags. I am asking you to stop clearing them from my login.

{staff2}

PROVENANCE · lot {n}

The catalogue will say "private collection, by descent". That is true as far as it goes. It does not go as far as the years 1939 to 1951, for which we have nothing.

The consignor would prefer that nobody asks. The buyer we have in mind will not.

{staff}

From: {staff2}
To: sale room staff

On Thursday there will be two telephone bidders on the evening's main lot. One of them is the consignor's brother-in-law. He is there to keep the price moving and he is not to win.

If he looks like winning, {staff} will have trouble with the line.

{staff2}

